&lt;p&gt;Box (NYSE:BOX) is the leader in Intelligent Content Management. Our platform enables organizations to fuel collaboration, manage the entire content lifecycle, secure critical content, and transform business workflows with enterprise AI. We help companies thrive in the new AI-first era of business. Founded in 2005, Box simplifies work for leading global organizations, including JLL, Morgan Stanley, and Nationwide. Box is headquartered in Redwood City, CA, with offices across the United States, Europe, and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining Box, you will have the unique opportunity to continue driving our platform forward. Content powers how we work. It’s the billions of files and information flowing across teams, departments, and key business processes every single day: contracts, invoices, employee records, financials, product specs, marketing assets, and more. Our mission is to bring intelligence to the world of content management and empower our customers to completely transform workflows across their organizations. With the combination of AI and enterprise content, the opportunity has never been greater to transform how the world works together and at Box you will be on the front lines of this massive shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY BOX NEEDS YOU &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Our EMEA Marketing team fuels pipeline growth, builds brand awareness, and brings the Box story to life across European markets. As a Marketing Placement Student with German language capability, you will be an integral part of our Go-To-Market (GTM) engine, collaborating across Regional Marketing (DACH, Northern Europe, France), Partner Marketing, Digital Media, and Performance Marketing to drive high-impact marketing programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;During this 12-month placement based at our EMEA HQ in London, you will experience first-hand how a high-growth cloud SaaS enterprise operates. You will gain end-to-end exposure across multi-channel campaigns, digital advertising, event planning, and social advocacy—helping plan and execute flagship events (like CIOWorks Europe and BoxWorks) and tailoring campaigns for the DACH and EMEA markets while building a strong foundation for your marketing career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 []&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with Regional Marketing Managers across DACH, Northern Europe, and France to understand sales challenges and translate them into effective regional campaigns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support the planning, execution, and follow-up for flagship internal and third-party events across EMEA (such as BoxWorks, CIOWorks Europe, and Content Cloud Summit).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with the Partner Marketing team to coordinate joint marketing campaigns and lead generation with strategic ecosystem partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-annotation-id=&quot;dde0e869-b16d-4a06-b79a-e79c8c102c85&quot; data-author-id=&quot;33100491917&quot;&gt;Assist in executing digital media and performance campaigns, including coordinating ad creative, tracking setup, and analyzing campaign performance metrics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage and drive the EMEA social media advocacy program, curating content in advocacy tools and communicating impact to wider sales teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coordinate landing page builds, email marketing campaigns, and webinar productions in close partnership with the Marketing Operations team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Act as the go-to team champion for creative brainstorming, cross-functional campaign support, and administrative operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Live the Box core value to &quot;Take risks. Fail fast&quot; by testing innovative marketing tactics, learning rapidly, and bringing fresh creative ideas to the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
